  "output": "I'll read the file first, then rewrite it with CRLF endings.The write landed with LF endings, not CRLF — the file-writing tool normalized the line endings. I'll try again with explicit carriage returns in the content.Not done — the file still has LF endings.\n\nThe `write_file` tool normalizes line endings to LF, so it can't produce CRLF no matter what I pass in. Both attempts wrote 116 bytes, identical to the original, and `od -c` shows `\\n` with no `\\r` before it.\n\nYour options:\n\n| Approach | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `write_file` tool | Cannot do it — normalizes to LF |\n| Shell (`sed -i 's/$/\\r/'`, `unix2dos`) | Works, but you excluded the shell |\n| `.gitattributes` with `*.bat text eol=crlf` | Fixes it on checkout for the Windows agent, no content rewrite |\n\nThe file is unchanged from where it started. If you want, I can do the conversion with the shell, or add the `.gitattributes` rule — say which.",
